{"kind":"dissent","text":"feedback on the content:\n* The 'connect github' section describes technically what it does, but this needs to be written in terms of the user's job-to-be-done. Describe the user's actual goals, actions and outcomes.\n* The 'current gitseq repository has no live charter...\" doesn't belong in a how-to instructional guide. Perhaps a short `status` header instead.\n* Before you configure it... you need (several impossible things). No. Item 1 is created by the process of configuring it, and so are 3 and 4.\n* \"Establish the charter and clauses\" section: again, this is meant to be documentation for a user whose goal is to connect their GitHub issues and PRs so that gitseq can be used to discuss and progress them. \"The connector refuses...\" is completely illegible to such a user.\n\nAnd so on. Rewrite for user readability, keeping in mind their goal, and how this helps them achieve it."}